{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n -i \"P60|full-corner|semifinite|Aristotle|closeout\" <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -80'","aggregated_output":"294:# Task Group: source-workspace two-lane Aristotle/Codex formalization autopilot\n296:scope: autonomous two-lane theorem formalization, terminal-status Codex closeout, safe artifact staging, and resource-bounded Lean verification\n297:applies_to: cwd=source-workspace; reuse_rule=reuse only after checking the live queues, `state.json`, systemd unit, Lean checkout, and Aristotle task state; no acceptance or advancement is implied by this partial rollout\n303:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, success: two-lane queues and compact manuscript staging verified)\n307:- Aristotle, Codex, `aristotle_autopilot.py`, autopilot.toml, FF15–FF23, P37–P46, `AUTOPILOT_ACCEPTED: yes`, `AUTOPILOT_DECISION: advance`, AUTONOMY_POLICY.md\n309:## Task 2: diagnose systemd and quarantine-closeout failures\n313:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, partial: recovered closeout path; FF15/P37 advancement unverified)\n321:- when the user said Aristotle may “develop necessary theory” or take “another easier route” -> permit project-local supporting theory and alternative recognizable proofs, but require explicit assumptions and no silent weakening [Task 1]\n327:- The live runner is `work/aristotle_autopilot/aristotle_autopilot.py`, configured by `work/aristotle_autopilot/autopilot.toml`. It has independent finite-fiber FF15–FF23 and stabilizer-hyperfinite P37–P46 queues, one active Aristotle task per lane, Codex closeout only at terminal status, and advancement only after both machine-readable acceptance and decision fields. [Task 1]\n330:- Persist closeout metadata in `work/aristotle_autopilot/state.json` before starting Codex. An interrupted closeout without a machine-readable decision halts for review rather than retrying or advancing ambiguously. [Task 2]\n334:- symptom: systemd reports `[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'codex'` and terminal Aristotle jobs never close out -> cause: the NVM executable is outside noninteractive PATH -> fix: set the absolute Codex path in both the service and runner, then verify the service environment. [Task 2]\n335:- symptom: a closeout consumes about 13 GB and clones/builds Mathlib -> cause: `lake build` was run in a stripped downloaded Aristotle quarantine snapshot with no `.lake` -> fix: inspect/quarantine there, copy only the reviewed candidate to the already-built live project, and run all Lean checks only in that live checkout. [Task 2]\n336:- status guard: at rollout end FF15 and P37 were still active. Do not claim candidate acceptance, FF15 integration, or FF16/P38 submission until `state.json`, closeout output/review, and live Lean checks agree. [Task 2]\n483:- thm:finite_projections_exist, full_tracial_corner_semifinite, central projection, qMq, fullness, formalization_finite_fibers, VonNeumannAlgebra\n495:## Task 3: locate the active package and interpret Aristotle task artifacts\n503:- magic_and_algebras, AristotleCandidates, aristotle_tasks, support-corner, finite-region Pauli, HANDOFF.md, realtime voice\n519:- when the user asked whether existing jobs were being generated by an Aristotle loop -> inspect concrete task IDs/status artifacts before acting; do not infer running work from noisy realtime transcription [Task 3]\n532:- symptom: Aristotle archive metadata claims commits/pushes or a queued FF15 result is treated as proof -> fix: independently compile candidate source in the live package, run axiom/trust scans, obtain both reviews, and only then integrate. FF15 remained pending in this rollout. [Task 2]\n568:- P47, P48, P49, P50, P51, SOT, WOT, bicommutant, Kaplansky density, GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean, aristotle_autopilot.timer, tg-send\n576:- when the user approved unattended automation and Telegram notifications -> halt and alert on blocked/failed/partial/unverified closeouts, but keep routine successful progress quiet [Task 3]\n580:- `B(H) \\bar⊗ R` has a tracial state only for finite-dimensional `H`; for infinite-dimensional `H`, its relevant trace is faithful normal semifinite and the factor is `II_∞`. [Task 1]\n591:- symptom: strong closedness is treated as density of the original C*-algebra -> fix: distinguish retention of limits in `M` from bounded approximants supplied by Kaplansky density. An attempted P49A/P49B/P49C plan patch failed context matching, so inspect `PLAN.md`, TOML, and `state.json` and make a narrow verified update before claiming those packets exist. Recheck `aristotle-autopilot.timer` after any queue migration. [Task 3]\n1370:- arXiv:2306.01837, Generalized entropy for general subregions in quantum gravity, geometric modular flow conjecture, H_xi^g, modular Hamiltonian, KMS, beta=2pi/kappa, admissible vector field, constant surface gravity, semifinite weight, pdftotext, curl\n1380:- The paper-specific normalization is `h_Psi=(2pi/kappa) H_xi^g`, equivalently KMS inverse temperature `beta=2pi/kappa`. A rigorous prompt should specify the algebraic setting, initial Cauchy surface, entangling surface, normal faithful state or appropriate normal faithful semifinite weight, KMS statement, and domain/self-adjointness assumptions [Task 1]\n1806:- For repo-root graph work, the quickest structural check is `python3 <original-home>/.codex/skills/project-graph-scheme/scripts/project_graph.py validate --graph project_graph.json`; closeout-quality verification then adds `python3 -m json.tool` on the JSON files, `jsonschema.validate(...)` or `jsonschema -i`, and locator audits when nodes point into real files [Task 2][Task 3][Task 4]\n1817:- symptom: graph closeouts overstate mathematical certainty -> cause: the graph is treated as a proof artifact instead of a provenance/navigation layer -> fix: state explicitly that the graph records the current support status and does not independently re-prove the mathematics [Task 2][Task 3]\n1898:- rollout_summaries/2026-07-15T13-22-01-YKcF-general_type_ii_stabilizer_criterion_workline.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/07/15/rollout-2026-07-15T15-22-01-019f65f1-0246-7c83-9c24-dd45127a4929.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-15T13:44:33+00:00, thread_id=019f65f1-0246-7c83-9c24-dd45127a4929, same rollout; distinct routing value for compile/verification and conditional-closeout guidance)\n1937:- symptom: first-pass LaTeX warnings look like unresolved problems at closeout -> cause: references only settle after a second pass -> fix: rerun `pdflatex` and report final-state warnings separately from first-pass noise [Task 2]\n2472:- Let `p=zq`. A faithful trace finite on the corner identity `p` makes `p` finite in `pMp` and hence in `M`: any `v` with `v^*v=p` and `vv^*<p` has `v=pvp\\in pMp`; traciality gives equal trace values while faithfulness gives `tau(p-vv^*)>0`, a contradiction. Normality is unnecessary; semifiniteness alone is insufficient. Local sources: Blackadar V.2.1.14, PDF p. 446; Kadison--Ringrose II Definition 6.3.1, PDF p. 41. [Task 2]\n2485:- symptom: finiteness is inferred from a merely semifinite trace -> cause: finite value on the corner identity was not checked -> fix: require a faithful trace with `tau(p)<infinity` and include the `v=pvp` transfer from `pMp` to `M`. [Task 2]\n2505:- Lean, mathlib, CStarAlgebra, WStarAlgebra, VonNeumannAlgebra, GNS, PositiveLinearMap.GNS, Pauli, partial-trace, support-corner, Kaplansky-density, ultraweak, semifinite, technical.tex\n2510:- for this stabilizer project, retain `G_F=G\\cap A_F` and broad proof-compatible conditional framing; do not turn a semifiniteness certificate into factoriality or type-`II_\\infty` classification [Task 1]\n2516:- Treat the support-corner-to-semifiniteness argument as a separate frontier: strong/strong-* topology, bicommutants, Kaplansky density, ultraweak normality, finite projections/central support, and full-finite-projection-implies-semifinite are not an integrated finished package. Defer central direct-integral/factor classification. Suggested staged interfaces: `finite_stabilizer_density_and_partial_trace`, `support_monotonicity_from_compatible_projector_states`, `abstract_support_corner_is_tracial`, `full_finite_projection_implies_semifinite`. [Task 1]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
