ha-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P55-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha-out-of-budget.md\n?? reviews/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor-closeout.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,300p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md; printf '\\\\n--- packet ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,320p' aristotle_tasks/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,300p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md; printf '\\\\n--- packet ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,320p' aristotle_tasks/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\nC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\nAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\nalgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\nunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\nboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\nanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\nreplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P50's checked WOT continuity is retained as a stronger\nconcrete certificate, but the field name alone is not accepted as a\nformalization of the standard ultraweak definition of normality. Package P50U\nmust define the ultraweak topology from absolutely summable series of matrix\ncoefficients, prove the topology comparison, and export an explicitly\nultraweak-normal P50 conclusion. This does not block P51's finite-projection\nargument, which uses the corner state's traciality and faithfulness rather than\nnormality.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: the original P55 is retired after Aristotle returned\n`OUT_OF_BUDGET` without creating `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean`. The failed\nrun is not evidence and no code from it is integrated. Lane H now uses four\nseparate gates: P55A constructs finite-stage Pauli-to-dyadic equivalences,\nP55B proves coherence and the finite/infinite direct-limit identifications,\nP55C constructs faithful source/regional operator representations and their\nclosed ranges, and P55D extends the algebraic alpha by density. This split is\nmathematical: P53 and P54 did not yet contain an identification between their\ntwo different algebraic direct limits. P56 depends on accepted P55D.\n\nP60 may run independently of Lane H after P51 and P50U. It is optional Lane-G\nstrengthening and must use P50U's literal ultraweak-normal corner state. It may\nassume an explicitly named countable comparison family for the full corner,\nbut it may not infer a global weight from fullness alone or conceal the weight,\nnormality, faithfulness, traciality, or semifiniteness laws in an axiom.\n\n--- packet ---\n# P60 — optional global semifinite weight from a full finite corner\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Infrastructure only:** optional strengthening beyond the Lane-G manuscript\n  conclusion; this packet makes no claim that the manuscript requires it.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P60`; Lane `G` optional strengthening.\n- **Predecessors:** `P51`, `P50U`, both integrated and locally audited before\n  submission.\n- **Gate discharged:** globalize a full finite corner to a faithful normal\n  semifinite weight under exact comparison/countability hypotheses.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no claim that P51 already supplied a global\n  weight, no direct-integral theorem, and no Lane-H factorization.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean`. Use P51's\nfull finite corner and P50U's literally ultraweak-normal faithful tracial\ncorner state. Under an explicit normalized countable comparison family of\npartial isometries whose source projections lie below `q`, whose pairwise\northogonal range projections sum strongly to `1`, and whose distinguished\nzeroth member has source and range projection `q`, define the ambient\nextended-positive trace/weight on the positive cone with values in `ℝ≥0∞` by\nthe corresponding monotone series of transported corner traces. Develop the\nsmallest project-local extended-positive-weight API required when pinned\nMathlib does not provide one.\n\nProve, from the displayed construction, additivity, positive homogeneity,\ntraciality, faithfulness, normality in the standard weight sense (preservation\nof suprema of increasing positive nets/sequences at the level supported by the\ndeveloped API), and semifiniteness. The global extended-valued weight is not a\nbounded linear functional, so do not define its normality as ordinary\nultraweak continuity on all of `M`; instead use P50U's ultraweak-normal bounded\ncorner functional to prove the monotone-supremum law. Also prove the value on\nfinite partial sums and that the global weight restricts exactly to the P50U\ntrace on `q M q`. Keep the separate theorem that fullness plus the exact\nsigma-finite comparison theorem produces the required countable family; if\nthat comparison theorem itself is unavailable, take only the countable family\nas a named hypothesis and do not claim it follows from fullness.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nList every comparison-family, orthogonality, normalization, and convergence\npremise explicitly. Normality,\nfaithfulness, traciality, and semifiniteness of the resulting weight are proof\ntargets, not permitted premise fields. The P50U corner normality theorem must\nbe used rather than the older WOT field name. Do not encode the desired global\nweight itself as an interface field or axiom.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean`; import P51\nand P50U.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n`lake build AristotleCandidates.FullCornerSemifiniteWeight` succeeds without\nforbidden declarations and reports the exact optional assumptions, the weight\ndefinition, and the declarations proving its required weight laws. A\ngenuine missing comparison theorem may remain conditional; the weight laws may\nnot be replaced by a bundled assumption.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
